---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout><div class="shell"><header class="nav"><a class="brand" href="/">stavlos<span> / the agent workshop</span></a><nav aria-label="Main"><a href="#team">The team</a><a href="#surfaces">The surfaces</a><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos">GitHub ↗</a></nav></header>
<main id="main-content"><section class="hero"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">PERSISTENT AGENTS. SHARED WORK.</p><h1>Good work takes<br><em>more than a turn.</em></h1><p class="lede">A local-first harness for coding agents that stay available. Start a conversation, build a team, and steer the work as it happens.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos#readme">Open the workshop ↗</a><a href="#team">Meet the working model ↓</a></div></div><aside class="work-order"><div class="order-top">WORK ORDER / ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLE<span>LOCAL</span></div><p class="order-title">Ship the next thing.</p><div class="agent-row"><span class="agent-mark">A</span><div><b>architect</b><p>Map the system. Coordinate the work.</p></div><span class="status">WORKING</span></div><div class="agent-row"><span class="agent-mark">E</span><div><b>explorer</b><p>Follow the implementation details.</p></div><span class="status">WORKING</span></div><div class="agent-row"><span class="agent-mark">R</span><div><b>reviewer</b><p>Stay ready for the next handoff.</p></div><span class="status">IDLE</span></div><div class="order-bottom"><span>ONE CHANNEL / A TEAM THAT STAYS</span><span>↳</span></div></aside></section>
<section class="model" id="team"><div class="model-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE WORKING MODEL</p><h2>Keep the thread.<br>Grow the team.</h2><p>Each agent has context and an inbox. A completed response leaves someone you can follow up with.</p></div><div class="model-list"><article><span>01</span><div><h3>Resume the conversation</h3><p>Global channels let you return to work. Conversations, tool calls and state changes are recorded in an append-only event log.</p></div></article><article><span>02</span><div><h3>Delegate when it helps</h3><p>Agents can create focused teammates, send messages and bring findings back. Children remain available for follow-up work.</p></div></article><article><span>03</span><div><h3>Steer while it runs</h3><p>Redirect an agent, cancel a turn, or stop it. Project trust, explicit permissions and a Linux sandbox define the boundaries.</p></div></article></div></section>
<section class="surfaces" id="surfaces"><p class="eyebrow">MORE THAN ONE WAY IN</p><h2>Choose your seat<br>at the workbench.</h2><div class="surface-grid"><article><b>01 / TERMINAL</b><h3>The command seat.</h3><p>Talk to agents, manage the team, and answer permission requests from the terminal UI.</p></article><article><b>02 / WEB</b><h3>A window on the work.</h3><p>A loopback web UI shows channels, conversations, sheets, questions and permissions. Answer questions and approvals in the terminal or Discord.</p></article><article><b>03 / DISCORD</b><h3>Keep the thread nearby.</h3><p>Connect a Discord client to take conversations, questions and permission responses into an existing communication surface.</p></article></div></section>
<section class="start"><div><p class="eyebrow">BRING YOUR OWN WORK</p><h2>A stable for<br>your next project.</h2><p>Sign in through supported subscriptions, including ChatGPT, Grok, Z.ai Coding Plan and Kimi For Coding. Follow the public guide for setup and requirements.</p></div><div class="source-card"><span>BUILD FROM SOURCE</span><pre>git clone https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos.git
cd stavlos
go install ./cmd/stavlos</pre><a class="button" href="https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos#readme">Read the setup guide ↗</a></div></section></main><footer><a class="brand" href="/">stavlos</a><p>Local-first agent harness · Built in Go</p><a href="https://github.com/nicodes/stavlos">Source ↗</a></footer></div></Layout>
